{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7165097","formula":"N₅⁺","hill":"N5","elements":["N"],"composition":{"N":5.0},"names":{"en":"Pentazenium","ru":"Пентазений"},"descriptions":{"en":"In chemistry, the pentazenium cation (also known as pentanitrogen) is a positively-charged polyatomic ion with the chemical formula N+5 and structure N−N−N−N−N. Together with solid nitrogen polymers and the azide anion, it is one of only three poly-nitrogen species obtained in bulk quantities.","ru":"Пентазений — это азотсодержащий катион в химии, состоящий из пяти атомов азота, соединенных последовательно. Его соединения являются перспективными для получения веществ с большой плотностью энергии, например N5[B(N3)4], N5[P(N3)6] или N5N3. Не следует путать с анионом N5− (пентазолат-анионом)."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":139031002,"mass":70.03,"charge":1,"smiles":"[N-]=[N+]=N[N+]#N","inchikey":"UXGCMSPHSBEHRM-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"139031002","atoms":5,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.949,"y":-0.55,"z":0.041,"el":"N"},{"x":1.064,"y":0.161,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":0.074,"y":0.894,"z":-0.042,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.101,"y":0.062,"z":-0.011,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.986,"y":-0.567,"z":0.012,"el":"N"}],"bonds":[[0,1,2.0],[1,2,2.0],[2,3,1.0],[3,4,3.0]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7165097","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pentazenium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9F%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B9","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/139